==English==

===Etymology===
Likely from {{m|en|ball}} in the sense of a dance.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-have a ball.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|have<has,,had> a ball}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[enjoy]] oneself thoroughly; to have lots of [[fun]] or [[excitement]].
#: {{ux|en|The kids '''had a ball''' playing in the fountain.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1973|artist={{w|Slade (band)|Slade}}|title=w:Merry Xmas Everybody|passage=Are you hanging up a stocking on your wall? / It's the time that every Santa '''has a ball''' / Does he ride a red-nosed reindeer? / Does a ton up on his sleigh / Do the fairies keep him sober for a day?}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1976|artist=w:ABBA|title=w:Money, Money, Money|passage=In my dreams I have a plan / If I got me a wealthy man / I wouldn't have to work at all, I'd fool around and '''have a ball'''}}
#* {{quote-song|en|author=w:J. G. Thirlwell|title=Sick Man|album=Hole|year=1984|artist={{w|Foetus (band)|Scraping Foetus Off the Wheel}}|text=His victim screams, he '''has a ball'''<br>The bigger the head, the harder they fall}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1998|artist=w:Baha Men|title=w:Who Let the Dogs Out|passage=When the party was nice, the party was jumpin' /  And everybody '''havin' a ball'''}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=H.H. Fuller|title=It's a Wrap|publisher=Writers Club Press|page=72|passage=“Well, after they retired down here, they must have '''had a ball''' ordering anything and everything.”}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2006|author=Chrigel Glanzmann|title=Your Gaulish War|artist=w:Eluveitie|album={{w|Spirit (Eluveitie album)|Spirit}}|passage=I hope you '''had a ball''' in effacing lives!}}
#* {{quote-song|en|year=2011|artist=w:Rebecca Black|feat=w:Patrice Wilson|title={{w|Friday (Rebecca Black song)|Friday}}|passage=Yesterday was Thursday, Thursday / Today i-is Friday, Friday / We-we-we so excited /  We so excited / We gonna '''have a ball''' today}}

